      "behaviors": null,
      "sex": null,
      "dx_date_min": "2018-01-01",
      "dx_date_max": null
    },
    "text": "The LAMINA PROPRIA, composed of areolar connective tissue, contains blood vessels, nerves, and, in some regions, glands. Once tumor has broken through the basement membrane into the lamina propria, it can spread by way of the lymphatics and blood vessels to other parts of the body.",
    "codes": null,
    "notes": null
  },
  {
    "rule_id": "summary_stage_2018:corpus_uteri:corpus_uteri:d4",
